You convert ONE file of a Node.js (CommonJS) Express backend from Sequelize/Postgres to Mongoose/MongoDB.
Hard rules:
1. Reply with ONLY the complete new file inside one ```javascript block. No explanations. No new npm packages.
2. Keep every exported name, every function signature, the same HTTP status codes, the same error classes
   (require("../helper/customErrors")) thrown in the SAME ORDER, and EXACTLY the same response JSON shapes.
   Preserve the original's observable behaviour, INCLUDING its bugs (if the original crashes with a 500 in some
   case, the new code must also throw there, after the same side effects).
3. Data access ONLY through `const { User, Article, Comment, Tag, Favorite, Follower, mongoose, nextId } = require("../models")`
   (path relative to the file). Models listed below. Prefer `.lean()` reads and build plain response objects
   explicitly; there is no `dataValues`, no `toJSON` magic, no Sequelize association methods.
4. Never send `_id`, `password`, `authorId`, `articleId` or internal fields to clients unless the response
   shape lists them. Users have integer `_id` (the old `id`). Comments expose `id` (= their integer `_id`).
5. New users/articles/comments get `_id: await nextId("users"|"articles"|"comments")`. Tags use the tag name as `_id`.
6. Compound `_id` documents (Favorite, Follower): READ/DELETE with dotted paths, e.g.
   `{ "_id.userId": a, "_id.followerId": b }`. INSERT (idempotent) ONLY with an exact `_id` filter, keys in exactly
   the listed order: `const key = { userId: a, followerId: b }; await Follower.updateOne({ _id: key },
   { $setOnInsert: { _id: key } }, { upsert: true, session })`. (A dotted-path filter + $setOnInsert of _id FAILS
   with "would modify the immutable field '_id'".)
7. Counters (`followersCount`, `favoritesCount`): change them ONLY when a junction document was really inserted
   (`res.upsertedCount === 1`) or deleted (`res.deletedCount === 1`), inside the same transaction:
   `const s = await mongoose.startSession(); await s.withTransaction(async () => { ...ops with { session: s }... }); await s.endSession();`
8. Sequelize timestamps map to Mongoose `timestamps: true` (createdAt/updatedAt are set automatically).
9. Build EVERY response object field by field, exactly as listed in RESPONSE SHAPES: never return or spread a
   database document (`res.json({ user: doc })` leaks `_id`, `createdAt`, `email`, `followersCount`...). Include a key
   only if the shape lists it for that endpoint.

MODELS (generated from the reviewed schema; you cannot change them):
- Article (collection articles): _id:Number(=Articles.id), slug:string, title:string, description:string, body:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, authorId:int, tagList:[String] (embedded TagList), favoritesCount:Number (counter of Favorites.articleId, YOU must $inc/$dec it). Indexes: {"slug": 1}; {"createdAt": -1}; {"authorId": 1, "createdAt": -1}; {"tagList": 1, "createdAt": -1}
- Comment (collection comments): _id:Number(=Comments.id), body:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, articleId:int, authorId:int. Indexes: {"articleId": 1}
- Tag (collection tags): _id:String(=tag name). Indexes: -
- User (collection users): _id:Number(=Users.id), email:string, username:string, bio:string, image:string, password:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, followersCount:Number (counter of Followers.userId, YOU must $inc/$dec it). Indexes: {"username": 1}; {"email": 1}
- Favorite (collection favorites): _id:{articleId,userId} compound. Indexes: {"_id.articleId": 1}; {"_id.userId": 1}
- Follower (collection followers): _id:{userId,followerId} compound. Indexes: {"_id.followerId": 1}; {"_id.userId": 1}

RESPONSE SHAPES the endpoints of this file must produce (from the original app):
- GET /api/articles/feed -> 200: {articles:[{author:{bio:str|null,followersCount:int,following:bool,image:str|null,username:str},body:str,createdAt:str,description:str,favorited:bool,favoritesCount:int,slug:str,tagList:[str],title:str,updatedAt:str}],articlesCount:int}
ORM BEHAVIOUR TO PRESERVE (found by the static analyzer):
- getFollowing(...) runs a JOIN through the junction table; the receiver may be null if the preceding findOne found nothing (=> TypeError => HTTP 500 in the original).
- findAndCountAll with `include` and no `distinct: true`: Sequelize's count counts JOINED ROWS. With a to-many include (tagList) an article with k>1 tags is counted k times (LEFT JOIN => an article with 0 tags counts 1). A filtered include (`where` on the include) becomes an INNER JOIN. The rewrite must reproduce this count.
- `offset: offset * limit` - the query parameter `offset` is a PAGE index, not a row offset. skip = offset*limit.
req.loggedUser (set by the converted auth middleware) is a lean User document WITHOUT email, with `_id`, username, bio, image, password, followersCount and `token`; it is undefined when no Authorization header was sent.
--- already converted helper/helpers.js (use its exports as-is) ---
const { User, Favorite, Follower, Tag } = require("../models");

const slugify = (string) => {
  return string.trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\W|_/g, "-");
};

const appendTagList = (articleTags, article) => {
  const tagList = articleTags.map((tag) => tag._id);
  if (!article) return tagList;
  article.tagList = tagList;
};

const appendFavorites = async (loggedUser, article) => {
  const articleId = article._id;
  const userId = loggedUser ? loggedUser._id : null;

  const favorited =
    userId &&
    (await Favorite.findOne({
      "_id.articleId": articleId,
      "_id.userId": userId,
    }).lean());

  article.favorited = loggedUser ? !!favorited : false;

  const favoritesCount = await Favorite.countDocuments({
    "_id.articleId": articleId,
  });
  article.favoritesCount = favoritesCount;
};

const appendFollowers = async (loggedUser, toAppend) => {
  const userId = loggedUser ? loggedUser._id : null;

  if (toAppend?.author) {
    const author = await User.findById(toAppend.author._id).lean();

    const following =
      userId &&
      (await Follower.findOne({
        "_id.userId": author._id,
        "_id.followerId": userId,
      }).lean());

    toAppend.author.following = loggedUser ? !!following : false;

    const followersCount = await Follower.countDocuments({
      "_id.userId": author._id,
    });
    toAppend.author.followersCount = followersCount;
  } else {
    const following =
      userId &&
      (await Follower.findOne({
        "_id.userId": toAppend._id,
        "_id.followerId": userId,
      }).lean());

    toAppend.following = loggedUser ? !!following : false;

    const followersCount = await Follower.countDocuments({
      "_id.userId": toAppend._id,
    });
    toAppend.followersCount = followersCount;
  }
};

module.exports = { slugify, appendTagList, appendFavorites, appendFollowers };


